{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"### [1/3] MEASURED FACTS — do not re-derive\n\nPROBLEM: tickets branch = 1.04 GiB; 92% is the reconciler .bridge_state cache. Object attribution on ONE 51-day denominator: bindings.json 828.3 MB (16.2 MB/day), prev_snapshot.json 228.1 MB (4.5), event *.json 55.0 MB (1.08), commits/trees 15.5 MB (0.30), other 25.8 MB (0.51, still unattributed).\n\nROOT CAUSE (measured): per-pass churn in bindings.json across consecutive committed revisions = baseline VALUE changed 0 entries; `baseline_advanced_at` (written once at binding_store.py:375, read NOWHERE in src/) changed 1144; `last_get_pass` changed 20. ~100% of growth is bookkeeping no consumer reads, scattered across a sort-ordered 18 MB file, defeating delta compression.\n\nFIX EFFECT (40 consecutive real revisions rebuilt in a clean repo, repacked --window=250 --depth=50, marginal = (pack_N - pack_1)/(N-1)):\n  as-committed  40/40 distinct versions  12.79 KB/version  499 KB\n  A1 only       40/40                     1.74 KB           68 KB  (7.4x)\n  A1 + A2       20/40                     2.05 KB           39 KB  (12.8x)\nCAVEAT: the measurement models A1 as DELETING the field. Since baseline value changes are 0, the write-when-changed guard is byte-neutral today - the measured win is the deletion.\n\nCLONE COST vs GitHub: full 1.04 GiB / 59s wall / 319s CPU; --filter=blob:none 68.7 MiB / 14.3s; --filter=blob:limit=1m 72.1 MiB / 13.2s. Whole-store verify-identity in a blob:none clone fetched 0 BYTES and ran FASTER than full (3.75s vs 3.98s): its scan is a pure tree-level diff and event/keyring bodies are read from the WORKING TREE (verify_authorship.py:371, authorship.py:119-128).\n\nprev_snapshot key-set (newest 400 revisions): 218/399 consecutive pairs have an IDENTICAL key set (become byte-identical, no commit); mean symmetric difference when it changes = 1.78 keys; key-set payload at HEAD = 19,960 bytes vs 27.1 MB full."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785371949681072001,"uuid":"3487d4f7-5a35-4fed-869f-10c5786ae0ac"}